# Build-time only. Committed on purpose — the Docker build copies this to
# .env.production, and `pnpm build` needs these names to resolve.
#
# Nothing here is a secret and nothing here reaches the image: the runtime stage
# copies only build/, node_modules/ and package.json — never .env.production. At
# runtime $env/dynamic/private reads process.env, supplied by the env_file (Docker)
# or the Helm values and chat-secrets Secret (Kubernetes).
#
# Two separate reasons a name has to be listed here:
#
# 1. $env/static/* imports are inlined at compile time, so the name must exist or the
#    build fails. PUBLIC_DELIVERY_API_BASE (ws.ts) is the only one left. Its value is
#    irrelevant to production — it is read solely under import.meta.env.DEV, which Vite
#    replaces with `false` in a production build, dead-code-eliminating the branch. The
#    value that matters for `pnpm dev` lives in .env.local.
#
# 2. src/lib/server/config.ts calls required() at module top level, and SvelteKit's
#    postbuild `analyse` step imports every server module to trace routes — which runs
#    that check during the build. Without the three API bases the build dies with
#    "Missing required environment variable: USER_API_BASE". These are placeholders,
#    NOT the values the app runs with. If the real ones are ever missing at runtime,
#    required() still throws on startup, as intended.

PUBLIC_DELIVERY_API_BASE=ws://localhost/chat

USER_API_BASE=http://build-time-placeholder.invalid/user
MESSAGE_API_BASE=http://build-time-placeholder.invalid/messaging
PRESENCE_API_BASE=http://build-time-placeholder.invalid

# Same reason: src/lib/server/jwt.ts derives JWT_SECRET_BYTES at module top level and
# calls .replace() on this, so an undefined value is a TypeError during `analyse`.
# THIS IS NOT A SECRET AND IS NEVER USED TO SIGN ANYTHING. The real value comes from
# the chat-secrets Secret at runtime; tokens signed with the string below would be
# rejected by every service in the system.
JWT_SECRET=not-a-real-secret-build-time-placeholder-only
